Note: OSC — Open Sound Control client + server, opt-in via `use "@osc"`
Note: Single-module surface for the 5 OSC builtins:
Note:   oscSend(String host, Int port, String path, ...args) → Void
Note:   oscListen(Int port, String path, Function handler) → OscHandle
Note:   oscStop(OscHandle handle) → Void
Note:   oscBundle(...packets) → OscBundle (varargs)
Note:   oscSendBundle(String host, Int port, OscBundle bundle) → Void
Note:
Note: Type-tag inference: Int→,i Long→,h Float→,f Double→,d
Note:   String/Symbol→,s Bool→,T/,F Buffer→,b. Charitable smallest-tag-that-fits
Note:   inference (composer can force via explicit cast at call site).
Note: Rate limit: per-path drop-newest sample-and-hold at 200 Hz
Note:   (5 ms window). No advisory on individual drops.
Note: Bundle nesting depth cap: collapses at 8 with stderr advisory (DoS guard).
Note:
Note: Implementation backed by Rug.Osc 1.2.5 — MIT, zero transitive deps.

module osc

use "@std"

Note: ===== Internal C# Function Declarations =====

Note: Marker builtin called once at module load (last expression of this
Note: file). Flips ExecutionContext.OscEnabled = true so the 5 surface
Note: builtins unlock. Composers should not call this directly — the
Note: trailing (__enableOscModule) line below handles it at import time.
internal proc __enableOscModule ()

Note: ----- Client builtins -----
internal proc oscSend (String: host, Int: port, String: path)
internal proc oscSendBundle (String: host, Int: port, OscHandle: bundle)

Note: ----- Server builtins -----
Note: oscListen returns an OscHandle reference-identity value.
Note: The handler lambda is invoked once per matching incoming message
Note: (rate-limited at 200 Hz/path drop-newest).
internal proc oscListen (Int: port, String: path, Function: handler)
internal proc oscStop (OscHandle: handle)

Note: oscPump runs any queued listener-handler invocations on the calling
Note: (foreground) thread and returns how many fired. Handlers from a real
Note: listener never run on the background receive thread — they are queued and
Note: drained here / on the next osc* call, serialized with the rest of the
Note: script so they cannot corrupt the interpreter. Call (oscPump) inside a
Note: poll loop that does not otherwise call osc* builtins.
internal proc oscPump ()

Note: ----- Bundle constructor (varargs) -----
Note: Returns an OscHandle-wrapped OscBundle. Bundles dispatch
Note: both ways with timetag honored on receive; outgoing bundles use
Note: OscTimeTag.Immediate (value 1) unless an explicit timetag is added
Note: at the send call.
internal proc oscBundle ()

Note: ===== Side-effecting init marker =====
Note: Flips ExecutionContext.OscEnabled = true so the 5 builtins above
Note: unlock. Without this line, every call to oscSend / oscListen /
Note: oscStop / oscBundle / oscSendBundle raises "requires `use \"@osc\"`".
(__enableOscModule)
